 Units Transfused From Baseline Through Week 26","description":"The number of units of PRBC transfusions was estimated. In one transfusion subjects received one or more units.","populationDescription":"The ITT set included all subjects assigned to treatment.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEDIAN","dispersionType":"Full Range","unitOfMeasure":"PRBC transfusions","timeFrame":"Up to Week 26","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Pegcetacoplan","description":"Subjects were received SC infusion of pegcetacoplan 1080 mg twice weekly or every 3 days up to end of the RCP (Week 26). Subjects were not allowed to receive treatment with other complement inhibitors."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Standard of Care","description":"Subjects continued to receive SoC treatment but were not allowed to receive treatment with a complement inhibitor unless they qualified for pegcetacoplan escape therapy."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"35"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"18"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0.0","lowerLimit":"0","upperLimit":"19"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"3.0","lowerLimit":"0","upperLimit":"13"}]}]}],"analyses":[{"groupIds":["OG000","OG001"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"<0.0001","pValueComment":"Wilcoxon rank-sum test p-value for the comparison between treatments is based on median using stratified non-parametric analysis. The 95% confidence interval (CI) is constructed using Hodges-Lehmann Estimation of Location Shift.","statisticalMethod":"Wilcoxon Rank-Sum Test","paramType":"Median Difference (Net)","paramValue":"3","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"2","ciUpperLimit":"4"}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy- (FACIT-Fatigue) Scale Score at Week 26","description":"The FACIT-Fatigue Scale is a 13-item Likert scaled instrument that is self-administered by the subjects during clinic visits. Subjects were presented with 13 statements and asked to indicate their responses as it applied to the past 7 days. The 5 possible responses are \"Not at all\" (0), \"A little bit\" (1), \"Somewhat\" (2), \"Quite a bit\" (3), and \"Very much\" (4). With 13 statements, the total score has a range of 0 to 52. The higher score corresponded to a higher quality of life. Baseline is defined as average of measurements prior to first dose of pegcetacoplan or on or prior to randomization of SoC. Post baseline missing values are imputed using multiple imputation method with Markov Chain Mont Carlo method.","populationDescription":"The ITT set included all subjects assigned to treatment.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Error","unitOfMeasure":"scores on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline and Week 26","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Pegcetacoplan","description":"Subjects were received SC infusion of pegcetacoplan 1080 mg twice weekly or every 3 days up to end of the RCP (Week 26). Subjects were not allowed to receive treatment with other complement inhibitors."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Standard of Care","description":"Subjects continued to receive SoC treatment but were not allowed to receive treatment with a complement inhibitor unless they qualified for pegcetacoplan escape therapy."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"35"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"18"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"7.78","spread":"1.210"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"3.26","spread":"2.113"}]}]}],"analyses":[{"groupIds":["OG000","OG001"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.061","pValueComment":"P-value for baseline, strata and treatment is from LS mean of proc mixed and proc mianalyze based on parameter estimates.","statisticalMethod":"ANCOVA","paramType":"LS mean difference","paramValue":"4.51","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"-0.21