mization of SoC. Post baseline missing values are imputed using multiple imputation method with Markov Chain Mont Carlo method.","populationDescription":"The ITT set included all subjects assigned to treatment.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Error","unitOfMeasure":"scores on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline and Week 26","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Pegcetacoplan","description":"Subjects were received SC infusion of pegcetacoplan 1080 mg twice weekly or every 3 days up to end of the RCP (Week 26). Subjects were not allowed to receive treatment with other complement inhibitors."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Standard of Care","description":"Subjects continued to receive SoC treatment but were not allowed to receive treatment with a complement inhibitor unless they qualified for pegcetacoplan escape therapy."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"35"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"18"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"18.90","spread":"2.909"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-2.85","spread":"5.703"}]}]}],"analyses":[{"groupIds":["OG000","OG001"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.0006","pValueComment":"P-value for baseline, strata and treatment is from LS mean of proc mixed and proc mianalyze based on parameter estimates.","statisticalMethod":"ANCOVA","paramType":"LS mean difference","paramValue":"21.75","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"9.35","ciUpperLimit":"34.16"}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Linear Analog Assessment (LASA) Scales Score at Week 26","description":"The LASA consisted of 3 items asking respondents to rate their perceived level of functioning. Specific domains include activity level, ability to carry out daily activities, and an item for overall QOL. Their level of functioning was reported on a 0-100 scale with 0 representing \"As low as could be\" and 100 representing \