treatment up to end of study (up to Week 79). A treatment-emergent serious adverse event (SAE) was a TEAE that met at least 1 of the following criteria: was fatal, life-threatening, required or prolonged inpatient hospitalization, resulted in persistent or significant disability/incapacity, was a congenital anomaly/birth defect, or was another medically important serious event.\n\nThe treatment-emergent events of interest (EOI) prespecified for this study included serious infections (meningococcus aspergillus, and other serious infections/sepsis), and infusion reactions.","populationDescription":"The safety analysis set included all treated participants, with treatment assigned based on actual treatment received.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","timeFrame":"Day 1 to End of Study (up to Week 79)","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"ABP 959","description":"Participants who received ABP 959 900 mg in Period 1 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks) or ABP 959 900 mg in Period 2 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 26 weeks)."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Eculizumab","description":"Participants who received eculizumab 900 mg in Period 1 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 52 weeks) or eculizumab 900 mg in Period 2 (administered IV every 14 ± 2 days for 26 weeks)."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"41"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"42"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"All TEAEs","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"33"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"39"}]}]},{"title":"Any Treatment-emergent SAE","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"7"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"2"}]}]},{"title":"Any Treatment-emergent EOI: Infusion reaction","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"15"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"15"}]}]},{"title":"Any Treatment-emergent EOI: Serious infection","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000",